        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): do not label finish_reason error as LLM timeout",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen OpenRouter (or Google via OpenRouter) finishes a stream quickly with `finish_reason: \"error\"`, OpenClaw classified that completed provider failure as a timeout. Operators saw **LLM request timed out.** with `failoverReason: timeout` / 408-class signaling, even when `durationMs` was only a few seconds and `rawErrorPreview` was `Provider finish_reason: error`. That sends people to timeout/network knobs that cannot fix a provider-completed error. Model fallback still ran; the bug is mislabeling and bad diagnostics.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Docs alignment\n\n`docs/concepts/model-failover.md` now states that bare OpenAI-compatible stop/finish reasons (`Unhandled stop reason: error`, `stop reason: error`, `reason: error`, `Provider finish_reason: error`) are **`server_error` (status 500)**, not timeout. Abort / `network_error` / `malformed_response` remain timeout (408).\n\n### Controlled provider stream → gateway boundary (after fix)\n\nProduction modules on this branch (`mapOpenAIStopReason` → `coerceToFailoverError` → `resolveModelFallbackError` → `formatAssistantErrorText`):\n\n```console\n$ ./node_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof-finish-reason-error-not-timeout.mjs\n=== Controlled provider stream (OpenAI-compatible finish_reason) ===\n  stream finish_reason=error → {\"stopReason\":\"error\",\"errorMessage\":\"Provider finish_reason: error\"}\n  stream finish_reason=network_error → {\"stopReason\":\"error\",\"errorMessage\":\"Provider finish_reason: network_error\"}\n\n=== Gateway failover boundary (production coerce/resolve) ===\n  bare finish_reason:error: {\"reason\":\"server_error\",\"status\":500,\"message\":\"Provider finish_reason: error\",\"modelFallbackKind\":\"failover\",\"advancesModelFallback\":true}\n  finish_reason:network_error: {\"reason\":\"timeout\",\"status\":408,\"message\":\"Provider finish_reason: network_error\",\"modelFallbackKind\":\"failover\",\"advancesModelFallback\":true}\n\n=== Classifier matrix (production modules) ===\n  {\"sample\":\"Provider finish_reason: error\",\"reason\":\"server_error\",\"isTimeout\":false,\"isProvider\":true}\n  {\"sample\":\"finish_reason: error\",\"reason\":\"server_error\",\"isTimeout\":false,\"isProvider\":true}\n  {\"sample\":\"stop reason: error\",\"reason\":\"server_error\",\"isTimeout\":false,\"isProvider\":true}\n  {\"sample\":\"Unhandled stop reason: error\",\"reason\":\"server_error\",\"isTimeout\":false,\"isProvider\":true}\n  {\"sample\":\"Provider finish_reason: network_error\",\"reason\":\"timeout\",\"isTimeout\":true,\"isProvider\":false}\n  {\"sample\":\"Provider finish_reason: abort\",\"reason\":\"timeout\",\"isTimeout\":true,\"isProvider\":false}\n  {\"sample\":\"Provider finish_reason: malformed_response\",\"reason\":\"timeout\",\"isTimeout\":true,\"isProvider\":false}\n\n=== User-facing copy (not timeout rewrite) ===\n  userFacing=\"Provider finish_reason: error\"\n\nRESULT: PASS — controlled stream: bare error → server_error/500/fallback; network_error → timeout/408/fallback; copy keeps provider signal\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Bare `finish_reason: error` / stop-reason `error` was matched by timeout patterns, rewritten to \"LLM request timed out.\", and classified as timeout/408 even for fast provider-completed failures (issue #109218).\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS 26.5.2, Node v26.5.0, worktree `/tmp/oc-109313` on branch `fix/finish-reason-error-not-timeout` at `09c934c02e4`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n\n  ```bash\n  cd /tmp/oc-109313\n  ./node_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof-finish-reason-error-not-timeout.mjs\n  ```\n\n- **Evidence after fix:** Terminal output under Evidence. Controlled OpenAI-compatible stream maps `finish_reason: error` to the production error string; the gateway failover boundary returns `reason=server_error`, `status=500`, `modelFallbackKind=failover`, and user-facing copy keeps `Provider finish_reason: error`. Contrast path `network_error` stays `timeout`/`408` with fallback still eligible.\n- **Observed result after fix:** Provider-completed bare `error` is failover-eligible `server_error` with accurate diagnostics; genuine transport finish reasons remain timeouts; docs match the classifier.\n- **What was not tested:** Live OpenRouter stream against a real API key (no credentials in this environment). The stop-reason mapper and failover boundary modules are the same production path the gateway uses after a provider stream ends.\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #109218.\n\nRemove bare `error` from timeout stop/finish patterns; add `isProviderCompletedErrorFinishReasonMessage` and classify as `server_error` before the timeout rewrite in `formatAssistantErrorText` and sanitize. Keep abort / network_error / malformed_response as timeout-like for #61281. Document the contract in `model-failover.md`. Controlled-provider proof covers classification, status, user copy, and model-fallback eligibility together.\n",
